<title>BELGIUM: EMU issues not on Commission agenda next week.</title>
<headline>EMU issues not on Commission agenda next week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>There are no issues pertaining to economic and monetary union (EMU) scheduled for the European Commission's meeting next Wednesday, a spokesman said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;There's nothing planned for the meeting,&quot; the spokesman said, adding the Commission would likely take up such matters after the informal ECOFIN in Dublin on September 21.</p>
<p>A budget stability pact, a new Exchange Rate Mechanism and the legal framework for the single currency are all on the agenda in Dublin.</p>
</text>
